 init_intro="Some work is too important to sit inside one organisation. Alongside AIDE stand two independent initiatives, each with its own leadership and its own history of showing up for people. Imran works with both — as Honorary Executive Director, Coach and Counsellor with ADK, and as Co-Founder and Honorary Executive Director with Islah Network.",
 inits=[("halima-sadia.webp","ADK · Anjuman Dukhtaran-e-Kashmir","Halima Sadia leads ADK as President","Some organisations are built around an idea. This one was built around years of showing up when people needed help most. Founded in 1996 by the late Haji Mirza Khurram Haider, ADK has served needy women and families across Kashmir and Pakistan for over thirty years. In the last ten years alone it has completed projects worth more than PKR 500 million, reaching over 3,000 families, through marriages, ration, clothing, home construction and small business support. Halima Sadia leads ADK as President. Imran Aslam serves as its Honorary Executive Director, Coach and Counsellor."),
        ("ammara-zaidi.webp","Islah Network","Syeda Ammara Zaidi founded Islah and leads it as President","Islah began in 2016 with a line that still guides every step: invest in people, create sustainable success. Today its schools in Bahawalgarh, Kahroor Pakka and Taxila teach 350 female students. Its programmes have carried economic support to more than 1,000 women and counselling and mental health support to more than 1,000 women more, through therapy centres in Bahawalpur, Bhimber, Taxila and Sialkot and online, alongside a stitching centre, adult education and the Doctors Desk. Syeda Ammara Zaidi founded Islah Network and leads it as President. Imran Aslam serves as its Co-Founder and Honorary Executive Director.")],
